{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1103575-optional-rules-for-resonance","id":1103575,"title":"Optional rules for Resonance","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-06-14T12:19:00-07:00","id":1103575,"title":"Optional rules for Resonance","content":"In <b>Book of Secrets</b>, the mechanics for personal Resonance (i.e., the traits on your character sheet) are to add dice to Arete rolls (1 or 2, 2 being for Strong or Overwhelming Resonance) or to an appropriate Ability or Background roll (one die per dot of Resonance), once per story. I'm fine with keeping the latter part; but I'm thinking of replacing the former with an expansion of the Resonance Magical Modifier: instead of a flat \u00b11 to the difficulty (depending on whether the Resonance helps or hurts), grant a \u00b11 difficulty for Faint or Subtle Resonance, a \u00b12 for Noticeable or Strong Resonance, or a \u00b13 for Overwhelming Resonance. This would apply whenever the Resonance helps or hurts the magick, not just once per story; and it would apply to all Resonance and Synergy, not just personal Resonance.<br /> <br /> Second, the Flavors of Resonance align with the Avatar Essences: Devotional Resonance goes with a Questing Essence; Elemental Resonance goes with a Primordial Essence; Stabilizing Resonance goes with a Pattern Essence; and Temperamental Resonance goes with a Dynamic Essence. This really ought to have been pointed out on p.132, when the Avatar is discussed; although it is mentioned on p.138, under \u201cIntimate Mysteries\u201d. As a house rule, I'm thinking of requiring that the flavor of the mage's first dot of Resonance must match the Avatar's Essence. (This isn't about how complex or simple people are; this is about the notion that Resonance emanates from the Avatar, at least initially.)<br /> <br /> Conversely, Synergy is more closely associated with Paradox and Quiet: if you incorporate Dynamic Synergies into your magic, a Paradox Backlash is likely to inflict you with Madness, with the nature of the Madness corresponding with the description of the Synergy. Likewise, Entropic Synergy encourages Morbidity while Stasis Synergy encourages Denial. In this house rule, mages tend <i>not</i> to have Synergy traits; and when they do, they tend to be temporary things that go away sooner rather than later unless they complement the mage's Resonance (p.132). OTOH, places and objects \u2014 things without Avatars \u2014 can have Synergy based on what kind of magic they've been exposed to, but do not have Resonance. (Again, house rule; and there may be some magic items that are an exception to this.) <br /> <br /> There's a section on Prime Magick and Resonance which says that if you use four or five dots of Prime, your Resonance is treated as if it were four or five dots in terms of its effects; in a similar way, I'm thinking that the Entropy Sphere (or rather, whatever name I can find for it once I've finished retooling it to encompass all three aspects of the Metaphysical Trinity; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/805755-the-fate-sphere\">Fate</a>, for now) should imprint a suitable Synergy on things when you use four or five dots of it. It's not (usually) based on the mage's traits, but rather on how you're using the Sphere: imparting Doom causes Entropic Synergy; imparting Luck causes Dynamic Synergy; and imparting Fate causes Stasis Synergy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 06-16-2017, 02:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}